\title{miraiWebR: Parallel Tasks on Background webR Workers with a 'mirai'-Compatible API}
\description{
The 'mirai' package evaluates R expressions asynchronously in background R processes. WebAssembly R has no processes, sockets or threads, so 'mirai' itself cannot run in webR. This package offers a subset of its interface -- daemons(), mirai(), mirai_map(), everywhere(), unresolved(), collect_mirai(), stop_mirai() and the m[] / m$data idioms -- on background webR sessions that the BAMDD with webR/brms/stanli application starts in Web Workers. Each worker is a complete R with the application's package library, so tasks run genuinely in parallel. A 'future' backend, plan(miraiWebR::webr_workers), makes the same workers available to future.apply, furrr and other 'future' clients. Features of 'mirai' without a webR counterpart stop with an error rather than being ignored.
}
